  "title": "Balancing Flexibility and Structure",
  "content": "Healthy parenting requires both structure and flexibility. Too much rigidity can create fear or rebellion, while too much flexibility can create chaos or insecurity. Children thrive when parents provide a stable foundation while also adapting to the child’s needs, emotions, and developmental stage.\n\nThis lesson explores how to find the balance between being firm and being responsive. Parents learn how to adjust routines during stressful times, how to offer choices within boundaries, and how to stay connected even when enforcing limits.\n\nFlexibility is not the opposite of structure—it is structure with empathy. When parents balance both, children feel supported and understood.",
